  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: 'What happens between multiple Hexamers?



'
    basic: As insulin concentration rises, more and more insulin hexamers bump into
      each other, tiling in three dimensions to form a crystal.
    intermediate: 
    advanced: "Insulin concentration reaches precipitation level in mature insulin
      vesicles. \n'Water jackets' around insulin hexamers form a hydrogen bonded
      network that interacts with other nearby hexamers. \nThe hexamer facilitates
      hexagonal packing.\r\n"
